Rolland Suh (rolland@MCS.COM) wrote:
: Hi,

: I am very new to VAX/VMS systems, so please pardon my ignorance.
: I would like to find out what does "Pathworks" do, and who
: manufactures it?  Is "Pathworks" some sort of driver for VAX
: machines?  What protocols does it support?  If I have "Pathworks"
: client loaded into a PC, can my PC talk to the VAX?  

Good question, Rolland - this is one of the most misunderstood things
about the product family; What it is!

PATHWORKS is a family of networking products written and sold by
Digital Equipment Corporation.


Servers:
PATHWORKS for OpenVMS(LanMan): Lan Manager 2.2 file & print server, 
 the NetBEUI protocol

PATHWORKS for OpenVMS(Netware): Netware file & print server, the
 IPX protocol

PATHWORKS for VMS(Macintosh): AppleShare file & print server,
 the AppleTalk protocol

PATHWORKS for OSF/1: Lan Manager 2.2 file & print server, and the 
 NetBEUI protocol

PATHWORKS for Ultrix: Lan Manager 1.3 (SMB) file & print server

PATHWORKS for SCO: LanManager 2.2 file & print server  


Clients:
PATHWORKS for DOS and Windows:  DECnet, TCP/IP, NetBEUI protocols, 
 LanManager client (redirector), IPX protocol, Netware client (shell),
 various DECnet and TCP/IP tools & utilitites, X11 Display server for
 DOS, network management tools, VMSMail client for DOS, LAT protocol,
 terminal emulator for DOS and Windows

PATHWORKS for Macintosh: DECnet, LAT & TCP/IP protocols, terminal emulator,
 X11 Display Server, VMSMail client


Both Server and Client:
PATHWORKS for OS/2: DECnet protocol (works with LanMan serv & client),
 LAT protocol, terminal emulator, assorted DECnet tools.

PATHWORKS for Windows NT: DECnet protocol (works with LanMan server & client),
 assorted DECnet tools


Hope this helps (and that I havn't left anything out!)

: How can I
: attatch a Mac LocalTalk network to a Pathworks network?  Do I 
: need a special router for that?  If I do, what kinds are recommanded?

You need a router to get from LocalTalk to Ethernet cabling; what protocols
it needs to run depend on what you're planning on doing with the Macintoshes
that are on the LocalTalk cable.  If you just want file & print services (from
your VMS system or other servers), you just need it to pass AppleTalk protocol.
If you also want to use VMSMail client, terminal emulation, XWindows, etc., 
then I'd recommend getting a multi-protocol router that does AppleTalk, DECnet,
and TCP/IP (FastPath, GatorBox, etc).

